Django Oscar Debian Package
===========================

Two packages are provided:

  python3-oscar        The framework library (for development)
  django-oscar-service Service infrastructure for running a site on a server

Getting started with django-oscar-service
------------------------------------------

1. Install the package and create your Django project:

   apt install django-oscar-service
   cd /var/lib/django-oscar/
   sudo -u www-data django-admin startproject myshop project/

2. Edit /var/lib/django-oscar/project/settings.py:

   Add Oscar's INSTALLED_APPS (see python3-oscar package docs), configure
   the database, set STATIC_ROOT='/var/lib/django-oscar/static/', and
   MEDIA_ROOT='/var/lib/django-oscar/media/'.

3. Configure the runtime environment in /etc/django-oscar/environment.conf:

   - SECRET_KEY is auto-generated on install
   - ALLOWED_HOSTS should list your domain(s)
   - Set DATABASE_* variables for PostgreSQL/MySQL if not using SQLite

4. Edit /etc/django-oscar/uwsgi.ini:

   Adjust the listening port (default 8080), process/thread count, and
   any path overrides needed for your project layout.

5. Enable and start the service:

   systemctl enable --now django-oscar.service

The service will auto-run migrations on each restart via ExecStartPre.

Adding products
---------------

Products are managed through the admin dashboard at /admin/ or imported
from CSV files using the oscar_import_catalogue management command.

Thumbnail backend
-----------------

This package uses sorl-thumbnail (python3-sorl-thumbnail). The
easy-thumbnails alternative is not available in Debian.

Directory structure
-------------------

/etc/django-oscar/                      Configuration files
/var/lib/django-oscar/project/         Your Django project directory
/var/lib/django-oscar/media/           Uploaded media files
/var/lib/django-oscar/static/          Collected static files
/var/run/django-oscar/                 Runtime directory (sockets)
